; compiler-newallox-fallback (#32): the button "INCREASE 150% -
; RECOMPILE" of the requester "Not Enough Object Memory Available!"
; (alloxinc -> newallox): when the larger buffers cannot be allocated,
; newallox falls back to the previous sizes and reports that as
; success, so the compile runs again with the same sizes, overflows
; again and shows the same requester, without a word about the memory.
; blitz2 under inject (alerts answered), a source whose code (20000
; statements through nested macros) overflows the default Object Buffer
; (16384 bytes); the allocation of the larger buffers (86016 bytes,
; MEMF_PUBLIC|MEMF_CLEAR) fails once.  COMPILE AND RUN (CREATE
; EXECUTABLE would make the buffers fit, Make Smallest), INCREASE 150%;
; COMPILE AND RUN again, CANCEL COMPILE; QUIT.  Correct: the out of
; memory alert after INCREASE, the compile ends, the second compile shows
; the requester again (the sizes are those before), blitz2 ends
; normally.  The original jumps out of the compile through TED's
; extalloc (#369) and its second compile does not come back.
; @fixed #32 Cc
; @file bo.bas "Macro a\na=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1:a=a+1\nEnd Macro\n"
; @file bo.bas "Macro b\n!a:!a:!a:!a:!a:!a:!a:!a:!a:!a\nEnd Macro\n"
; @file bo.bas "!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n"
; @file bo.bas "!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n"
; @file bo.bas "!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n!b:!b:!b:!b:!b\n"
